    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d203">

                <pb facs="0291" n="277" sameAs="frus:frus1948v06/pg277"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">501.BC
                    Indonesia/7–648: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            Consulate General at Batavia</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-07-06T19:00:00-04:00">July 6, 1948—7 p.
                            m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>320. Usgoc 119. Reports from Lake Success reach
                    Dept to effect that Critchley preparing new action designed to surmount present
                    impasse negotiations. Dept uninformed character such action. In order to avoid
                    prejudice position new USDel and for other
                    reasons Dept hopes you will reserve your position Aus suggestion pending Dept’s
                    receipt details and your receipt Dept’s comments thereon.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Marshall</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
